# compromise_overlay.log — a SMALL, clearly-labeled teaching overlay appended to
# the REAL loghub OpenSSH log (data/OpenSSH_2k.log) at demo time ONLY.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: the real loghub OpenSSH_2k.log is pure internet brute-force
# noise — it contains ZERO successful logins. That is realistic, but it kills
# the lab's core lesson ("a success from an IP that was ALSO brute-forcing is a
# compromise, not a coincidence"). These two lines re-introduce that exactly one
# signal WITHOUT altering the real dataset: an `Accepted password` from
# 187.141.143.180 — the single most prolific brute-force source IP in the REAL
# log above. Same hostname (LabSZ) and `Dec 10` timeframe as the real entries so
# the overlay reads as one continuous log.
#
# This is the only synthetic content in the lab; everything else is the real
# public capture. Do not treat these two lines as real-world data.
Dec 10 09:45:11 LabSZ sshd[26041]: Accepted password for fztu from 187.141.143.180 port 51330 ssh2
Dec 10 09:45:11 LabSZ sshd[26041]: pam_unix(sshd:session): session opened for user fztu by (uid=0)
